{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "6f2a1a10-6c1e-4c2b-9a3f-2b8b1a9d1c01",
		"name": "Saheli Backend — Auth & Profile",
		"description": "Authentication (phone + OTP) and Profile CRUD for the Saheli Spring Boot backend.\n\n**Flow to run in order (Auth folder):**\n1. Register User — creates an unverified User row and issues an OTP\n2. Verify OTP (Register) — verifies the OTP, marks the user verified, returns access + refresh JWT\n3. Login User — for an already-verified phone, issues a fresh OTP\n4. Verify OTP (Login) — same endpoint as verify, returns fresh tokens\n5. Refresh Token — exchanges a refresh token for a new access + refresh pair\n\nAll tokens/ids are captured automatically into collection variables by each request's Tests script, so requests can be run top-to-bottom with the Collection Runner.\n\n**Profile folder** requires `accessToken` to be set (run the Auth flow first). Auth is inherited at the collection level as a Bearer token using `{{accessToken}}`; the four Auth requests explicitly opt out of it since `/api/auth/**` is public.\n\nOTP demo mode is on by default in local dev (`OTP_DEMO_MODE=true`) — every OTP is `123456` and is echoed back in the response as `devOtp`, which the Register/Login requests capture into `{{otp}}` automatically.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
