						"description": "One-time onboarding: creates the `UserProfile` row for the authenticated user (updates `name`/`email` on `User`, uploads `profilePhoto` to S3 if provided, sets `isCompleted=true`). Requires a `USER`-typed Bearer access token. Success response is the plain string `Profile Saved Successfully` (no longer echoes the user id, as of commit `5d863d5`).\n\nMultipart request — `profileRequest` must be attached as a **text part with Content-Type: application/json** (not a query param, not top-level JSON body), and `profilePhoto` as a **file part**. In Postman, select a file for the `profilePhoto` key before sending.\n\n**`preferredLanguage` note (known gap, not yet fixed in code):** `ProfileRequestDto.preferredLanguage` was annotated `@NotBlank` in commit `5d863d5`, but the controller's `@RequestPart(\"profileRequest\") ProfileRequestDto profileRequest` parameter has no `@Valid`/`@Validated` — Spring does not run bean validation on a `@RequestPart` without it, so this constraint is currently a no-op. Omitting `preferredLanguage` does **not** return a clean 400; it either fails as a 500 (null hits the `preferred_language VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL` column) or silently persists an empty string, depending on whether the JSON key is missing vs. sent as `\"\"`. See the two error examples below."
